I want to display the actions being performed on each item to the user.
When the list is long, it would be best to display the log of this list processing for the user.
So I want to insert the log (string form) at last line of the Listbox after each run of the loop.
I don't want to clear the previous entries or override them (it would simply scroll onto the new entry when the loop continues).
I want each new string to appear as the last line of my ListBox as the loop progresses. I've tried using .insert(END, "") in tkinter Listbox but it deletes everything rather than inserting new entries. I want to keep them and just show the newly appended ones.
Here is an example of what I am doing:
import tkinter as tk

