    root.update_idletasks()
    root.update()

root.mainloop()

This works fine, but it erases everything and the list starts from the new line.
How can I preserve the old entries and append new ones at the bottom?

A: Your approach is almost correct, the mistake you're making is in not redefining the listbox after the loop, instead of appending more data to it. Try the following code:
import tkinter as tk

root = tk.Tk()

listbox = tk.Listbox(root)
listbox.pack()

for i in range(10):
    listbox.insert(tk.END, "Processing item " + str(i))
    root.update_idletasks()
    root.update()
    # Refresh the listbox after each iteration
    listbox.yview(tk.END)  

root.mainloop()

with listbox.yview(tk.END), you just scroll the listbox to the end of the list, keeping every previous message.

